Review proceedings in Germany are governed by Sections 160 et seq. of the German Act against Restraints of Competition (GWB).

A request for review is inadmissible if:
– the alleged infringement of procurement rules was not notified to the contracting entity without undue delay after the complainant became aware of it (§ 160 (3) No 1 GWB);
– infringements that were identifiable prior to expiry of the deadline for requests to participate or tenders were not notified by that date (§ 160 (3) No 2 GWB);
– more than 15 calendar days have elapsed after receipt of the contracting entity’s notice that it does not intend to remedy the complaint (§ 160 (3) No 4 GWB).

After dispatch of the award decision to the bidders, the contract may not be concluded before expiry of a standstill period of 10 calendar days (§ 134 GWB).
